---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base>
  <section class="page">
    <h1 class="kicker">Get Involved</h1>
    <p class="quote">“Each of you should use whatever gift you have received to serve others, as faithful stewards of God’s grace in its various forms.”</p>
    <p class="subtitle">1 Peter 4:10</p>
    <p>This is your parish. Every ministry needs people. Contact Mary Meissner, (719) 542-9248 ext. 111, mmeissner@ctkpueblo.org, to sign up.</p>
    <img src="/images/get-involved.jpg" alt="Parishioners serving at Christ the King" class="hero-image" />

    <h2>Liturgical ministers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Lector</strong> — Proclaim the readings at Mass after preparation and training.</li>
      <li><strong>Extraordinary Minister of Holy Communion</strong> — Assist with distributing Communion at Mass (and sometimes to the homebound).</li>
      <li><strong>Altar server</strong> — Help the priest and deacon so the liturgy flows smoothly and with reverence.</li>
      <li><strong>Usher</strong> — Greet people, assist with the collection, and help the liturgy run smoothly.</li>
      <li><strong>Hospitality</strong> — Welcome newcomers and offer a friendly presence to everyone who comes.</li>
      <li><strong>Music ministry</strong> — Sing or play to support the congregation’s praise (choir, cantor, or instrument).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Teaching and formation</h2>
    <p class="note">Volunteers who work with children or youth must complete Safe Environment training and a background check.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Catechist or aide for children</strong> — Share the faith with children in parish formation programs.</li>
      <li><strong>Catechist or aide for youth</strong> — Walk with teens in discipleship and formation.</li>
      <li><strong>Adult formation</strong> — Help lead or support Bible studies, small groups, and adult sessions.</li>
      <li><strong>OCIA team</strong> — Accompany adults who are becoming Catholic or completing their sacraments.</li>
      <li><strong>Vacation Bible School</strong> — Help with the week-long summer program for children.</li>
      <li><strong>Family formation sessions</strong> — Assist with family-based formation gatherings and meals.</li>
      <li><strong>Youth events and retreats</strong> — Support service days, retreats, and other youth activities. Contact Sarah Nelson (ext. 121, snelson@ctkpueblo.org) or Zack Garduno (ext. 114).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Prayer and care of the church</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Prayer line</strong> — Pray for the intentions shared through the parish prayer network. Contact Sarah Nelson (ext. 121, snelson@ctkpueblo.org).</li>
      <li><strong>Care of the narthex prayer spaces and votive candles</strong> — Dust statues, clean and refill votive candles, and keep the devotional spaces ready.</li>
      <li><strong>Adoration hour coverage</strong> — Sign up for a regular hour of Eucharistic Adoration (sign-up available in the narthex or via the current parish link).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Works of mercy</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Pueblo Soup Kitchen</strong> — Contact Executive Director Kathy Cline at 719-545-6540.</li>
      <li><strong>Sangre de Cristo Hospice</strong> — Call 719-542-0032.</li>
      <li><strong>Posada family shelter</strong> — Call 719-545-8776.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Seasonal projects and drives (especially during Advent, Lent, and Thanksgiving) are announced in the bulletin and on the parish website.</p>

    <h2>Parish organizations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Altar and Rosary Society</strong> — Support the beauty and care of the church and parish social life.</li>
      <li><strong>Knights of Columbus</strong> — Catholic men’s organization focused on charity, unity, fraternity, and patriotism.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .quote {
  text-align: center;
  font-style: italic !important;
  font-size: 1.1rem;
  line-height: 1.6;
  margin: 0.4rem 0 0.8rem;
}

.subtitle {
  text-align: center;
  font-weight: bold;
  font-size: 1.1rem;
  line-height: 1.6;
  margin: 0.4rem 0 0.8rem;
}
.hero-image {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  max-height: 420px;
  object-fit: cover;
  border-radius: 6px;
  margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
}
h1 {
  text-align: center !important;
  color: var(--gold);
  font-weight: 600;
  margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  padding-bottom: 0.6rem;
}
  .note {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0.75rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .page {
      padding: 8px 4px 40px;
    }

  }
</style>
